  "notes": {
    "c0003.md": "# Nora Vance / Vance Realty Group\n\nGreat client. Approves things fast and never once asked what a reshoot or an\nextra design round actually cost - which is exactly why nobody checked either.\n\n- Phase 1 signed at 18,600. Subcontractor budget was assumed at 9,400 in the\n  quote. Actual freelancer invoices came to 14,500.\n- Margin on phase 1 came in at roughly 8 percent against a 35 percent target.\n- Phase 2 is already underway. Lock every subcontractor quote in writing\n  before booking anyone this time.\n",
    "p0001.md": "# Vance Realty rebrand and campaign\n\nRed, closed. Revenue 18,600 - a real, solid contract by any deal-board\nmeasure. Subcontractor cost once everything was counted: 14,500 (Jules'\nreshoot and extra edit rounds, Sasha's brand set, Marcus's media setup, a\nrush copywriting fee that was never in the original scope). Priya's own time\ncost another 2,550 at the standard rate. Profit: about 1,550. Margin: 8.3\npercent against a 35 percent target.\n\nNothing about this project looked wrong while it was happening. The deal was\nwon, the client was happy, every invoice got paid. The leak was entirely in\nwhat delivery cost once it was subcontracted out, and nobody added it up\nuntil the job was already closed.\n"
  }
}
